#: ../../source/concepts.md:5
msgid "Ecliptic Longitude"
msgstr "# Concepts astrologiques"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:7
msgid ""
"**Ecliptic longitude** is the position of a celestial body measured along "
"the ecliptic (the Earth's orbital plane around the Sun), expressed in "
"degrees from 0° to 360°."
msgstr ""
"La **longitude écliptique** est la position d'un corps céleste mesurée le "
"long de l'écliptique (plan orbital de la Terre autour du Soleil), exprimée "
"en degrés de 0° à 360°."

#: ../../source/concepts.md:9
msgid "0° = Vernal point (0° Aries)"
msgstr "### Coefficients des harmoniques"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:10
msgid "90° = Summer solstice (0° Cancer)"
msgstr "#### Aspect Soleil-Lune (Conjonction)"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:11
msgid "180° = Autumn equinox (0° Libra)"
msgstr "#### Harmonique 2 (180°/2 = 90°)"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:12
msgid "270° = Winter solstice (0° Capricorn)"
msgstr "#### Aspect Soleil-Lune (Conjonction)"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:14
msgid "Ecliptic Latitude"
msgstr "### Latitude écliptique"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:16
msgid ""
"**Ecliptic latitude** measures the angular distance of a body above (+) or "
"below (-) the ecliptic plane."
msgstr ""
"La **latitude écliptique** mesure la distance angulaire d'un corps au-dessus"
" (+) ou en-dessous (-) du plan de l'écliptique."

#: ../../source/concepts.md:18
msgid "Distance in AU"
msgstr "### Distance en UA"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:20
msgid ""
"The **Astronomical Unit** (AU) is the average Earth-Sun distance, "
"approximately 149.6 million km."
msgstr ""
"L'**Unité Astronomique** (UA) est la distance moyenne Terre-Soleil, environ "
"149,6 millions de km."

#: ../../source/concepts.md:22
msgid "Astronomical Time"
msgstr "## Temps astronomique"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:24
msgid "Coordinated Universal Time (UTC)"
msgstr "### Temps Universel Coordonné (UTC)"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:26
msgid ""
"**UTC** is the reference time standard, based on international atomic time."
msgstr ""
"Le **UTC** est le standard de temps de référence, basé sur le temps atomique"
" international."

#: ../../source/concepts.md:28
msgid "Julian Day"
msgstr "### Jour Julien"

#: ../../source/concepts.md:30
msgid ""
"The **Julian Day** (JD) is a continuous dating system used in astronomy. JD "
"begins at noon UTC on January 1, 4713 BCE in the proleptic Julian calendar."
msgstr ""
"Le **Jour Julien** (JD) est un système de datation continue utilisé en "
"astronomie. Le JD commence à midi UTC le 1er janvier 4713 av. J.-C. du "
"calendrier julien proleptique."

